@startuml
title Discovering capabilities and reading configuration

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "Control application" as Client
participant "GATT service" as Gatt
participant "Protocol decoder" as Protocol
participant "Configuration manager" as Manager

Client -> Gatt: Read custom policy capabilities
Gatt -> Manager: Get build and controller capabilities
Manager --> Gatt: capabilities
Gatt --> Client: 61-byte value via GATT read / long read

Client -> Client: Select only supported custom command,\nsection, policy, and values
Client -> Gatt: Enable response indications
Client -> Gatt: Write get_configuration\n(request_id, section ID)
Gatt -> Protocol: Decode command
Protocol --> Gatt: Typed get_configuration
Gatt --> Client: ATT write response
Gatt -> Manager: Read selected section
Manager --> Gatt: configured_* value
Gatt -> Client: Indicate configuration_response\n(request_id, section variant)
Client --> Gatt: Confirmation

alt Client requests an unknown section ID
    Client -> Gatt: Write get_configuration
    Gatt --> Client: ATT write response
    Gatt -> Manager: Validate section ID
    Manager --> Gatt: command_result(unsupported)
    Gatt -> Client: Indicate configuration_response
    Client --> Gatt: Confirmation
end

note over Client,Gatt
An encoded command can be structurally valid yet semantically unsupported.
Only malformed binary payloads are rejected directly with an ATT error.
end note
@enduml
